  englishName: Longjing Shrimp
  chineseName: 龙井虾仁
  pinyinName: Longjing Xiaren
  category: 1
  difficulty: 2
  briefDescription: Stir-fried river shrimp with Dragon Well tea leaves.
  detailedDescription: A representative dish of Hangzhou cuisine. The meat of the live river shrimp is white and tender as jade, and the tea leaves are emerald green and fragrant.
  historicalOrigin: Famous since the 1940s, combining two famous Hangzhou products.
  culturalSymbolism: Symbolizes clarity and elegance.
  regionalSignificance: Showcases the use of local tea ingredients in cooking.
  craftmanshipNotes: Shrimp must be peeled by hand and stir-fried quickly.
  estimatedDuration: 300
  cookingSteps:
  - stepNumber: 1
    title: Peel Shrimp
